            "title": "Your Body Has Been Trying to Fix Your Sleep. Your Mouth Keeps Undoing It.",
            "body": "Your nose was built for breathing. It warms, filters and humidifies every breath before it reaches your lungs. Your mouth does none of that. When it falls open at night, your breathing turns shallow and ragged, and you wake up foggy and dry-mouthed. Not because you slept too little, but because you breathed the wrong way. NightSeals keeps your lips gently sealed so your nose can do its job all night.",
