          "type": "reason",
          "settings": {
            "number": "2",
            "title": "A Journalist Taped His Mouth Shut for Science. What He Found Changed How We Sleep.",
            "body": "Journalist James Nestor spent ten days breathing only through his mouth for a Stanford study. His snoring climbed, his sleep fell apart, and he felt terrible. When he switched back to nasal breathing, it reversed within a day. He wrote about it in his bestseller Breath, and it's the same simple principle NightSeals is built on. One strip. One night.",
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/ChatGPT_Image_Jul_24_2026_02_27_26_AM.png",
            "placeholder": "Add an image"
          }
        },
        "reason_3": {
          "type": "reason",
          "settings": {
            "number": "3",
            "title": "Why Thousands Chose This Over Every Other Sleep Fix They'd Tried",
            "body": "A better pillow. Melatonin. An earlier bedtime. Most people have tried them, and most are still tired, because none of them fix the actual problem. NightSeals does one thing: it keeps your mouth closed so you breathe the way your body was designed to. SteadyHold™ adhesive grips through a full beard without ripping; AirWeave™ mesh stays breathable all night. Simple, and it stays put.",
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/ChatGPT_Image_Jul_23_2026_12_59_00_AM-Photoroom.png",
            "placeholder": "Add an image"
          }
        },
        "reason_4": {
          "type": "reason",
          "settings": {
            "number": "4",
            "title": "The #1 Question Everyone Asks: \"What If I Can't Breathe?\"",
            "body": "Fair question. Short answer: you're not sealed shut. NightSeals uses a breathable AirWeave™ mesh and a gentle adhesive. A light effort parts your lips, and it peels off in a second. It's a reminder, not a lock, and your instincts always win. It's made for healthy adults who can breathe comfortably through their nose. It isn't for children, and it isn't a treatment for sleep apnea. If you suspect a breathing disorder, talk to your doctor first.",
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/ChatGPT_Image_Jul_24_2026_12_47_15_AM.png",
            "placeholder": "Add an image"
          }
